                6,
                7
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Medication:",
              "snippet": "Antidepressants can be helpful in alleviating depressive symptoms. Consult with a doctor or psychiatrist to determine if medication is appropriate for you.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                0,
                1,
                10,
                11
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "2. Engage in Self-Care:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "list": [
            {
              "snippet": "Prioritize Sleep: Establish a regular sleep schedule and create a relaxing bedtime routine.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                5,
                6
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Exercise: Engage in regular physical activity, even a short walk each day can boost your mood.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                5
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Healthy Eating: Focus on a balanced diet and stay hydrated.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                2,
                3,
                5,
                8
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Limit Alcohol and Drugs: These substances can worsen depression and should be avoided.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                3
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Engage in Enjoyable Activities: Make time for activities that bring you joy and relaxation.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                5
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Journaling: Writing down your thoughts and feelings can help you process emotions and identify negative thought patterns.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                6
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "3. Manage Social Connections:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "list": [
            {
              "snippet": "Stay Connected: Don't isolate yourself. Make an effort to connect with friends and family.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                2,
                6
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Seek Support: Join support groups or connect with others who understand what you're going through.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                4,
                6
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "4. Be Patient and Kind to Yourself:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "list": [
            {
              "snippet": "Recovery Takes Time: Be patient with yourself and celebrate small victories along the way."
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Focus on the Positives: Try to shift your focus to the positive aspects of your life and celebrate your progress.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                3
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "5. Make Lifestyle Adjustments:"
        },
        {
